  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure in place and centered over the forecast area will\ncontinue to keep dry and cool conditions in place through the\nperiod. Thus, fog and frost production will persist this morning\nbefore dissipating by 13Z. The clear skies with the new air mass\nin place with calm winds will make for isolated frost Wednesday\nmorning. The frost potential then backs off a bit through the\nrest of the week. Although, the NBM's performance of\ntemperatures has been trending a degree or two too warm and\ndecided to use the 25th percentile low temperatures for this\nmorning and Wednesday morning. This will mean that the frost\npotential will mainly be confined to Forest County for Thursday\nmorning and Friday morning. \n\nEnsembles have been consistent with the return of rain by\nSunday. Mid level ridging is expected to swing a tropical system\nfrom the western Gulf north into the Ohio Valley. This will\nbring precip north into the forecast area by Sunday night. While\nthis is a ways out and some details can change, the mean\nsolution is showing 0.40 to 0.70 of precip. The 75th percentile\nof this solution ups the totals to an inch. Certainly nothing\nconcerning at this point but bears watching.",
